# Response headers for brand.ijosh.com. Pages applies these to static assets.
#
# Five minutes everywhere: the paths are unversioned, and a redraw must reach every
# consumer without any of them redeploying. Bandwidth is unlimited on Pages, so there is
# no reason to cache harder.
#
# /mark/* carries no X-Robots-Tag on purpose. ijosh.com's favicon candidates live there,
# and Google requires that Googlebot-Image be able to crawl a favicon it is to use.
# Whether it would still use a noindex image is undocumented; the favicon is the reason
# this origin exists, so it is not risked. /tokens.css is unrestricted for the same
# reason: ijosh.com imports it, and Google is explicit that a page it cannot fetch the
# CSS for renders wrong. The line is what another site needs in order to draw itself.
#
# The index page, the banners and the photos are noindex -- a search for the name should
# return ijosh.com, not this. Nothing fetches a profile banner to render a page with, so
# /social/* has no reason to make the exception /mark/* and /tokens.css make.

/
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

/photo/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

/social/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

/mark/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

/tokens.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
